import Polyfold
/-! Blind formalization of V2_17 (the text's §2.2, Theorem 2.16, p. 25).

Text: (for an M-polyfold `X`) for every `m ≥ 0` the space `X_m` is metrizable, in particular
paracompact; `X_∞` is metrizable.  (The remark on the proof — Smirnov's theorem, Lemma 2.56,
Proposition 2.57 — is not part of the claim.)

Choices:
- Setting: `X : Type` (spaces put in `Type`, as asked; the project's `MPolyfold` is
  universe-polymorphic, so this is the instance `u = 0`) with `[TopologicalSpace X] [T2Space X]
  [ParacompactSpace X]` and an M-polyfold structure `P : MPolyfold X` (Definition 2.13: a
  paracompact Hausdorff space with an sc-smooth atlas; the project's `MPolyfold`, checked with
  `#print`: an `MAtlas` of pairwise compatible charts covering `X`, whose chart notion I checked).
- `X_m` with its topology (the paragraph after Definition 2.14: the points `x` with
  `φ(x) ∈ O_m` for a chart `φ`, topologized by the sets `φ⁻¹(W)`, `W` open in `O_m`) is the
  project's `P.Level m` with `P.levelTopology m` (checked with `#print`: the subtype
  `P.levelSet m` with the topology generated by the sets `{x ∈ V | lift of φ(x) to E_m ∈ W}`, `W`
  open in `E_m`, over the charts `φ` of the maximal atlas; the generating family the text
  describes, up to using all compatible charts, which gives the same topology).  The topology is
  passed explicitly to `MetrizableSpace` / `ParacompactSpace`.
- `X_∞ = ⋂ X_m` (`P.SmoothLevel`, the subtype of `P.smoothSet = ⋂ m, P.levelSet m`, checked) is
  given the inverse-limit topology: the coarsest topology making every inclusion `X_∞ → X_m`
  (`P.smoothIncl · m`, checked) continuous, `smoothTopology P` below.  This is my reading of the
  topology of `X_∞` (equivalently, the one generated by `φ⁻¹(W)`, `W` open in `O_∞` with the
  Fréchet topology of `E_∞`); I did not use whatever instance the project puts on `SmoothLevel`.
- "in particular paracompact" is stated as a separate conjunct.
-/
namespace RoundTrip.V2_17
open Polyfold

/-- The inverse-limit topology on `X_∞`: the coarsest one making all inclusions
`X_∞ → X_m` continuous. -/
@[instance_reducible] def smoothTopology {X : Type} [TopologicalSpace X] [T2Space X]
    [ParacompactSpace X] (P : MPolyfold X) : TopologicalSpace P.SmoothLevel :=
  ⨅ m : ℕ, TopologicalSpace.induced (fun x : P.SmoothLevel => P.smoothIncl x m)
    (P.levelTopology m)

/-- Every level `X_m` of an M-polyfold is metrizable and paracompact, and `X_∞` is metrizable. -/
def B : Prop :=
  ∀ (X : Type) [TopologicalSpace X] [T2Space X] [ParacompactSpace X] (P : MPolyfold X),
    (∀ m : ℕ,
      @TopologicalSpace.MetrizableSpace (P.Level m) (P.levelTopology m) ∧
      @ParacompactSpace (P.Level m) (P.levelTopology m)) ∧
    @TopologicalSpace.MetrizableSpace P.SmoothLevel (smoothTopology P)

end RoundTrip.V2_17
